              ["rispondere", "risposto", "avere"],
              ["bere", "bevuto", "avere"]
            ]
          }
        ],
        "notes": [
          "Most verbs use avere. Many verbs of movement or change of state use essere: andare, venire, arrivare, partire, entrare, uscire, tornare, restare, nascere, morire, diventare. So do all reflexive verbs: \"Mi sono alzato.\"",
          "With essere, the participle agrees with the subject: \"È nato\" (he was born), \"È nata\" (she was born), \"Sono nati\", \"Sono nate\".",
          "With avere, it usually stays -o, but it agrees with lo, la, li, le before the verb: \"L'ho vista\" (I saw her)."
        ]
